1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,738
Every new wall tile scores points right away.

2
00:00:03,058 --> 00:00:04,466
Let's learn to count them.

3
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:06,831
Here is Ana's wall.

4
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:08,538
A row goes across.

5
00:00:09,666 --> 00:00:11,096
A column goes down.

6
00:00:11,899 --> 00:00:13,777
Let's start with an empty wall.

7
00:00:15,149 --> 00:00:17,091
A new tile lands in row two.

8
00:00:17,411 --> 00:00:18,712
It has no neighbours.

9
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:24,206
A neighbour is a tile right beside it: left, right, above or below.

10
00:00:24,526 --> 00:00:25,614
No neighbours?

11
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:27,342
It scores one point.

12
00:00:29,549 --> 00:00:32,451
This tile touches the first one only at a corner.

13
00:00:32,771 --> 00:00:34,115
Corners don't count.

14
00:00:34,435 --> 00:00:36,163
So it scores one point again.

15
00:00:37,266 --> 00:00:38,162
New wall.

16
00:00:38,482 --> 00:00:41,128
Two tiles sit side by side in row two.

17
00:00:42,916 --> 00:00:45,156
The new tile lands right beside them.

18
00:00:45,476 --> 00:00:48,441
Count the unbroken line across: three tiles.

19
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:51,145
So it scores three points.

20
00:00:51,465 --> 00:00:54,153
Unbroken means no empty space in between.

21
00:00:56,349 --> 00:00:57,245
New wall.

22
00:00:57,565 --> 00:01:00,445
This time, the new tile lands right below a tile.

23
00:01:00,765 --> 00:01:02,515
Count down: two tiles.

24
00:01:02,835 --> 00:01:03,795
Two points.

25
00:01:04,899 --> 00:01:05,795
New wall.

26
00:01:06,115 --> 00:01:07,267
Look at row one.

27
00:01:07,587 --> 00:01:10,041
There is an empty space between these tiles.

28
00:01:11,849 --> 00:01:13,876
The new tile lands at the left end.

29
00:01:14,196 --> 00:01:16,095
An empty space stops the count.

30
00:01:16,415 --> 00:01:18,740
Only two tiles count: two points.

31
00:01:19,866 --> 00:01:20,826
The big one.

32
00:01:21,146 --> 00:01:23,898
This new tile will have neighbours across and down.

33
00:01:25,683 --> 00:01:27,560
Count across: four tiles.

34
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,651
Count down: three tiles.

35
00:01:30,766 --> 00:01:32,515
Add them: four plus three.

36
00:01:32,835 --> 00:01:33,966
Seven points!

37
00:01:34,286 --> 00:01:36,355
The new tile counts in both lines.

38
00:01:37,466 --> 00:01:40,069
Tip: tiles next to other tiles score more.

39
00:01:40,389 --> 00:01:42,095
So build your wall in groups.

40
00:01:43,199 --> 00:01:44,095
Remember.

41
00:01:44,415 --> 00:01:47,061
A tile with no neighbours scores one point.

42
00:01:47,381 --> 00:01:51,925
Otherwise, count the unbroken line across, and the unbroken line down.

43
00:01:52,245 --> 00:01:53,525
Add them together.

44
00:01:53,845 --> 00:01:55,423
Next: the next round.
